  "note": "Election of the whole Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1923; twelve members returned unopposed (Northern Whig, 6 January 1923, p. 6). 'There were nominations for the 12 seats Cookstown Urban Council ... all whom are Unionists, returned unopposed.' The paper prints no party label against individual names. Returned unopposed."
